Have you noticed that just walking down stairs moves a player to the next 
level? Also, they're not balanced: A player can escape from any monster just 
by running away. And any damage done by falling down stairs can be 
completely avoided, just by making several trips.

So here's my suggestions:
* Stairs shouldn't work all the time. There should be a 2/3 chance that 
nothing happens, and monsters get a free attack while the player is 
attempting to use them. Maybe they are really long stairs.

* They shouldn't be free. The Stair Troll could charge a fee to use them, 
taking either a percentage of gold (with a minimum of oh 100 zorkmids), or a 
magic item from inventory.

* They should be sometimes trapped. Searching and untrapping works, because 
it takes time, and will probably spring the trap anyway.

* They should be sometimes generated cursed. With cursed stairs several 
things can happen:
1. Nothing - player loses turn
2. Teleport - stairs just empty player somewhere else on level (one way 
trip, no MR applicable)
3. Level Teleport - plus/minus up to three levels.
4. Player arrives confused for a short period, disoriented by the windy 
stairs. 




